>
  <p>You want a straighter smile. The question is: clear aligners or traditional braces? Both are effective, but they work differently — and one might be a much better fit for your lifestyle. Here's what Fallbrook patients need to know before making the choice.</p>

  <h2>Invisalign®: The Clear Choice</h2>
  <p>Invisalign uses a series of custom-made, clear plastic aligners that gradually shift your teeth. Each set is worn for 1–2 weeks, then swapped for the next in the series.</p>

  <h3>Pros</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nearly invisible</strong> — most people won't notice you're wearing them</li>
    <li><strong>Removable</strong> — eat whatever you want, brush and floss normally</li>
    <li><strong>More comfortable</strong> — smooth plastic instead of metal brackets and wires</li>
    <li><strong>Fewer office visits</strong> — no wire-tightening appointments</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cons</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Requires discipline — must wear 20–22 hours per day</li>
    <li>Not ideal for very complex orthodontic cases</li>
    <li>Removable means you can lose or forget them</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Traditional Braces: Tried and True</h2>
  <p>Metal or ceramic brackets bonded to teeth, connected by wires that are periodically tightened to move teeth into position.</p>

  <h3>Pros</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Effective for even the most complex cases</li>
    <li>No compliance issues — they're always working</li>
    <li>Often less expensive than Invisalign</li>
    <li>Modern braces are smaller and more comfortable than ever</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cons</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Visible metal in your smile</li>
    <li>Food restrictions (no popcorn, gum, hard candy)</li>
    <li>Harder to brush and floss around brackets</li>
    <li>More frequent office visits for adjustments</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Which Is Right for You?</h2>
  <p><strong>Choose Invisalign if:</strong> you're an adult or teen who wants a discreet option, your case is mild to moderate, and you're committed to wearing your aligners consistently.</p>
  <p><strong>Choose braces if:</strong> your case is complex, you're younger and don't mind the appearance, or you worry about the discipline required for removable aligners.</p>

  <h2>Cost & Financing</h2>
  <p>Both options are comparable in cost for most cases. At Downtown Dental Studio, we accept CareCredit and Cherry financing to make orthodontic treatment affordable. Many insurance plans cover Invisalign at the same level as traditional braces.</p>

